# What `docker compose build` is NOT sent. The build context is the whole repo
# root (the apps need packages/shared), and without this file every build
# shipped - and `COPY apps/<app>` copied into an image layer - anything lying
# around on the server: node_modules and .next from a local `npm install`,
# uploaded caregiver documents, database backups, the git history, and the
# env files with every secret in them. Each rebuild then stored a fresh copy
# of all that in the build cache.
#
# The Dockerfiles install dependencies and build everything themselves, so
# nothing below is needed inside an image.

# The mobile app is built by Expo (EAS), never by these images, and no
# Dockerfile copies it.
apps/mobile

# Dependencies and build output - rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo

# Secrets - never in an image or the build cache
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env*.example

# Data that lives on the server, not in the code
storage
backups
.deploy

# Version control and editor/OS clutter
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Repo files no image uses
*.zip
*.patch
i18n-review
**/__tests__
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
DEPLOYMENT.md
IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md
WHATSAPP_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md
learn-codebase-complete.md
